### Agent name and link

Ante - https://github.com/AntigmaLabs/ante

### Where does it store sessions?

```
~/.ante/sessions/
```

Home-relative on every OS — there is no XDG / `AppData` / `~/Library` variant. `ANTE_HOME` overrides the root, so sessions land at `$ANTE_HOME/sessions/` when it is set.

Verified on Linux x86_64 with `ante 0.preview.76`. Related paths, not sessions: `~/.ante/projects/<cwd-slug>/memory/` (slug = absolute path with `/` replaced by `-`, e.g. `-home-user-Lab-proj`) and `~/.ante/logs/`.

### File format

**One directory per session**, named by a prefixed ULID:

```
~/.ante/sessions/
├── ses_01KZS4YPSNKG7CHK46XR0SVRX8/   # top-level session
│   ├── meta.json      # summary record — everything a session list needs
│   ├── dialog.json    # conversation state, rewritten in full on each save
│   └── events.jsonl   # append-only event log, one JSON object per line
└── suba_01KZS50N2Y0SB4Y3P58MJYWG78/  # subagent session — a SIBLING dir, not nested
    ├── meta.json      # adds "parent": "ses_..."
    └── dialog.json    # some subagent dirs have no events.jsonl at all
```

There is **no index file** — enumerate directories. `ses_*` = interactive session, `suba_*` = subagent spawned by the `Agent` tool, linked upward via `meta.parent`. 36 session dirs on my machine; largest `dialog.json` 4.0 MB, largest `events.jsonl` 2.7 MB.

