Title, cwd, model, tokens, duration and start time are all here, so a list view never has to open the large files. `first_user_message` is truncated by ante to ~160 chars with a trailing `...`.

#### dialog.json

A single object holding the state sent to the model — not a transcript:

```json
{
  "system": ["You are Ante, an agent developed by Antigma Labs..."],
  "tools": [ { "name": "Read", "description": "...", "input_schema": { ... } } ],
  "messages": [ ... ],
  "counted_messages": 6,
  "total_tokens": 34490
}
```

Note `input_schema`, not `parameters`. `system` is an **array of strings** (6 segments in my sample, the largest 33 KB).

Messages are Rust serde **externally-tagged enums**: the variant name is capitalized and is the single key of an object.

```json
{ "role": "User",  "content": { "Text": "hello" } }
{ "role": "Model", "content": { "Parts": [ ... ] } }
```

`role` is `"User"` or `"Model"` — not `assistant`. `content` is either `{"Text": "..."}` or `{"Parts": [...]}`. Part variants, with counts across my 36 sessions:

| part | n | shape |
|---|---|---|
| `ToolUse` | 1989 | `{id, name, args}` |
| `ToolResult` | 1989 | `{tool_use_id, content: {"Text": "..."}, is_error}` |
| `Thinking` | 884 | `{text, signature}` |
| `Text` | 582 | plain string |

`args` and `ToolResult.content` are free-form per tool — no fixed schema. Built-in tool names: `Agent`, `Bash`, `Edit`, `Glob`, `Grep`, `Read`, `TodoWrite`, `WebFetch`, `WebSearch`, `Write`, plus MCP tools as `mcp__<server>__<tool>`.

#### events.jsonl

Append-only, written live, and the better source for a timeline or usage view. Every line is `{timestamp, id, event, parent}` where `timestamp` is RFC3339 UTC with nanoseconds, `id` is an `evt_` ULID, and `parent` is an `op_` ULID identifying the turn.

| variant | payload |
|---|---|
| `UserInput` | string |
| `AgentMessage` | string |
| `Thinking` | string |
| `Info` | string (e.g. `"Trimmed 3 oversized tool results (45.1 KB) to fit the context window"`) |
| `TurnStart` / `TurnResume` | `{turn_id}` |
| `TurnPause` | `{turn_id, reason: {Approval: {tools: [...], message}}}` |
| `TurnEnd` | `{turn_id, status, steps}` |
| `ToolStart` | `{id, name, args}` |
| `ToolEnd` | `{tool_use_id, status, result_json}` |
| `UsageUpdate` | `{usage: {input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_tokens}, context: {used_tokens, limit_tokens}}` |
| `SessionUpdated` | `{model: {id, description, context_limit, effort, support_vision, weight_class}, provider: {id, display_name, base_url}, session_id, cwd, permission_mode}` |
| `CompactStart` | *(unit variant — see below)* |
| `CompactEnd` | `{summary}` |
| `SessionEnd` | `{session_id, reason, usage}` |

#### Gotchas a parser will hit

1. **Unit variants serialize as a bare string.** `CompactStart` is `"event": "CompactStart"`, not an object. Anything doing `Object.keys(line.event)[0]` throws on it — this bit me while exploring with `jq`.
2. **Status fields are string-or-object.** `TurnEnd.status` is `"Completed"`, or `{"Interrupted": {"reason": "turn cancelled"}}`, or `{"Error": {"kind": "auth", "headline": "authentication error", "details": ["HTTP 403 Forbidden", ...]}}`. `ToolEnd.status` in contrast is always a plain string: `"Completed"` (2015), `"Failed"` (96), `"Cancelled"` (5).
3. **`ToolEnd.result_json` is structured, tool-specific JSON**, not a string, and it carries its own nested variant that can disagree with the outer status. A failing `Bash` call gives `status: "Failed"` with `result_json: {"Completed": {"exit_code": 101, "stderr": "..."}}` — outcome detection must use the outer `status`, not the inner key.
4. **`Thinking.signature` is provider-dependent**: a long base64 blob on Anthropic-style providers, `null` on others (xAI in the attached sample).
5. **`counted_messages` != `message_count`** — the sample has `counted_messages: 6` in `dialog.json` and `message_count: 9` in `meta.json`.
6. **Compaction loses history from `dialog.json`.** It is post-compaction state, so a compacted session's `messages` array is far shorter than what actually happened; only `events.jsonl` keeps the full record (`CompactEnd.summary` was 28 KB in one of my sessions).
7. **Model and provider change mid-session** via `/model`, emitting `SessionUpdated`. `meta.model` is only the *last* model used, so per-message model attribution needs the event log.
8. **Torn reads on live sessions.** `meta.json` / `dialog.json` are whole-file rewrites and `events.jsonl` is appended, so expect a truncated final JSONL line and a briefly stale `dialog.json`.
9. **Subagent trees need a scan.** Reconstructing parent/child means reading every `suba_*/meta.json` for `parent`; nothing in the parent session's own files lists its children.

