In stream and skim layouts, the per-message metadata line (token counts, turn timing, and timestamp) disappears. For example, a line like `41.6k ctx / 468 out [ turn 7.4s · 2 calls ] Sep 2, 04:48 PM` is visible in default and compact modes but gone in stream and skim.

This seems unintentional since those modes are designed to strip the chrome (role badges, avatars) for a compact view, but the presence of the token/timing/timestamp metadata gets caught up in that streamlining.

The cause is in `MessageList.svelte` — both layouts set `display: none` on `.message-header`, which contains `.header-meta` (tokens, timing, timestamp) as a child:

```css
.layout-stream :global(.message-header) {
    display: none;
}

.layout-skim :global(.message-header) {
    display: none;
}
```

The intent is to hide the role chrome (avatar, label, copy/pin buttons) for a cleaner reading view, but the metadata gets caught in the same rule.

One fix: move `.header-meta` out of `.message-header` so it can stay visible independently, or target only the role elements instead of the entire header.
